{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"b737b1cb6ed9a36943d8ae58b46fc4e0b765df25a1697fa50bb3c714ea1b0199","digest":{"component_or_area":"ticket store mutation (_store/push.py)","key_entities":["_store/push.py","_resolve_conflicted_pop","refs/stash","git stash create","git stash apply","_store/event_append.py:_recover_from_unmerged","gitutil.path_is_foreign_to_branch","rebar tracker-maintenance",".tickets-tracker","origin/tickets",".bridge_state/","refs/rebar-maintenance/"],"problem_keywords":["git stash","shared stash stack","linked worktree","ticket store corruption","index stranding","worktree-local vs repo-global operations"],"propositions":["git stash operations in the tickets worktree use a shared repo-global stash stack that can apply entries created by other worktrees, causing index corruption and store wedging","the stash-merge-pop dance in push.py can leave unmerged entries and no MERGE_HEAD when a foreign stash is applied, blocking all subsequent ticket writes","the store must be mutated only through rebar's API, never through direct git operations like stash/commit/merge in the tracker, to prevent pollution with source files and state that do not belong on the tickets branch","foreign paths (source files, non-ticket content) ending up in an unmerged index must be auto-discarded rather than wedging the store, while genuine ticket-data conflicts must still refuse and surface"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787761169543104001,"uuid":"2b0e038b-dd69-4140-99d1-327c8b47703a"}